A leanbh, troubled sleep is a heavy thing to carry. A tea of chamomile and a little valerian root before bed might ease ye — 'tis an old remedy I give to many a weary soul. But if the dreams hold a darkness that herbs cannot touch, ye'd best speak with Father Kearney, for matters of the spirit are his province, not mine.

